.TH NOME 1 "2026-10-25" "nome 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nome \- switch between Linux distros and their user data, without root
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nome
.br
.B nome
.I NAME
.RI [ COMMAND ...]
.br
.B nome get
.I DISTRO
.RI [ NAME ]
.br
.B nome add
.I NAME ROOTFS
.br
.B nome cp\fR|\fBmv\fR
.I OLD NEW
.br
.B nome mount
.I NAME HOST\fR[:\fIGUEST\fR]
.br
.B nome umount
.I NAME PATH
.br
.B nome mounts
.I NAME
.br
.B nome
.RB { ls | distros | rm
.IR NAME | update | help | version }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nome
manages profiles. A profile is a persistent Docker container with a Linux distro in it,
plus a private home directory on the host that is mounted as /root. Docker (or podman, see
.BR NOME_DOCKER )
must be installed and running.
.PP
Run without arguments for a guided, colored text interface. Otherwise
.B nome mo ls
runs
.B ls
inside profile
.BR mo ;
with no command it starts
.B bash
(or
.B sh
if bash is missing).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B nome
Start the guided TUI: enter, install, add or delete profiles.
.TP
.BI nome " NAME " [ COMMAND ...]
Run COMMAND in profile NAME, or an interactive shell. The exit status is the command's.
.TP
.BI "nome get " DISTRO " " [ NAME ]
Create profile NAME (default: DISTRO) from a ready-to-use distro or any Docker image, e.g. ubuntu:20.04.
.TP
.B nome distros
List downloadable distros: alpine, ubuntu, ubuntu22, debian, arch, fedora, rocky, opensuse, kali, void.
.TP
.BI "nome add " "NAME ROOTFS"
Import an existing extracted root filesystem as a new profile.
.TP
.BI "nome cp " "OLD NEW"
Duplicate a profile, including installed packages and data.
.TP
.BI "nome mv " "OLD NEW"
Rename a profile.
.TP
.BI "nome mount " "NAME HOST" [: GUEST ]
Share a host folder with the profile. GUEST defaults to /mnt/<folder name>.
.TP
.BI "nome umount " "NAME PATH"
Stop sharing; PATH is the host or the guest path.
.TP
.BI "nome mounts " NAME
List the folder shares of a profile.
.TP
.B nome update
Replace this binary with the latest release for the current architecture.
nome also checks for new releases at most once a day (interactive use only) and prints a one-line notice.
.TP
.B nome ls
List profiles.
.TP
.BI "nome rm " NAME
Delete a profile: its container, image and data.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.nome/NAME/home
Private user data, mounted as /root. Survives recreating the container.
.TP
.I ~/.nome/NAME/binds
Extra bind mounts, one HOST:GUEST per line (managed by nome mount).
.TP
.I ~/.nome/NAME/image
The image the container is rebuilt from.
.PP
New profiles ask whether to mount the host root at /host; the default is yes.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Sessions start with a clean environment: only TERM is passed to the container.
.PP
Variables read by nome itself:
.TP
.B NOME_DOCKER
Container engine command (default: docker; podman works).
.TP
.B NOME_NO_UPDATE_CHECK
Disable the daily update check.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colored output.
